[{:db/id "q-22011/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "dfd79b53-cd56-5dfc-9979-b27d3d102d76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22011/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "6a698bda-6e9a-5e86-93ce-5485a0a270cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22011/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6718f0ba-1315-5099-8b1f-9dda88175b42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22011/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "dc4894a8-96a8-5034-a841-1ceacc27922c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22011/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "e78b2263-c151-5f34-8c9f-69ee87eef710" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22011/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa3728f-5676-5271-a84b-087affe49287" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-22011/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-22011/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-22011/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-22011/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-22011/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-22011/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-22011" :question/id #uuid "58e760c4-f329-5e64-bec0-d19376ff7221" :question/math-academy-id "q-22011" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(-6)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-6$" :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=-6$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}(x+6)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =-6,0,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-6,0,6.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=-6.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=72x-4{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=-6$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-6)=432>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=-6,$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-6)<0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=-6\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-22011/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-22016/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "1c74a4ee-dc9e-5f77-8ecb-9f24edddc9bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22016/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "ba4f430f-a020-5a09-90b9-3042fd43018c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22016/selection/c878bcdb91a0a5248ccd2809513b6e178833edd108ada4349638294858cbf7f2" :answer/id #uuid "33d84df6-752c-5b1e-bf98-6c7d80b66dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22016/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "a2f9fb7d-1b47-56ca-9dc4-21f64726f4e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22016/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "db81d32c-97fd-5a6f-90d6-0cec9d1c1a75" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22016/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "48b03e45-4e65-5aa0-a4a6-c1500340df7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-22016/selection/c878bcdb91a0a5248ccd2809513b6e178833edd108ada4349638294858cbf7f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-22016/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-22016/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-22016/selection/c878bcdb91a0a5248ccd2809513b6e178833edd108ada4349638294858cbf7f2" "q-22016/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-22016/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-22016" :question/id #uuid "d1f3f815-5705-5ffe-8f6e-280bb7f8ac8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-22016" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+36x+12.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+36x+12,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-60x+36.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=36{x}^{2}+24x-60.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =36(1)^{2}+24(1)-60=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. Solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-60x+36 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-5x+3) & =0 \\\\ 12(x-1)({x}^{2}+2x-3) & =0 \\\\ 12(x-1)(x-1)(x+3) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=-3$ and $x=1.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-4,0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-4) & =12(-4-1)^{2}(-4+3)=-300<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =12(0-1)^{2}(0+3)=36>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =12(2-1)^{2}(2+3)=60>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $-3$ | $(-3,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-4$ |  | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |  | $↗$ |\n\nAt $x=1,$  the first derivative does not change the sign. Therefore, $x=1$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-22016/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22016"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
